.TH AITERM.CONF 5 "2026-10-23" "aiterm 0.9.13-epsilon" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
aiterm.conf \- AITerm configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration file stores provider selection, encrypted credentials,
database connection settings, appearance, and runtime feature preferences.
The application rewrites the file when saving configuration; comments and
manual formatting may be lost. Back up the file before editing it manually.
.PP
The preferred starting point is the distributed
.I aiterm.conf.example
file. Restrict access to the file because it contains encrypted credentials
and operational configuration.
.SH FILE LOCATION
AITerm selects the first existing file in this order:
.IP 1. 3
The path named by AITERM_CONFIG.
.IP 2. 3
.I /etc/.UID.aiterm.conf
where UID is the numeric user ID.
.IP 3. 3
.I ~/.config/aiterm.conf
.IP 4. 3
.I ~/.aiterm.conf
.IP 5. 3
.I /etc/aiterm.conf
as the fallback path.
.SH FORMAT
The file is plain text with one key=value entry per line. Lines beginning with
# are comments. Values are generally read as text and converted according to
the option. Boolean/integer switches commonly use 1 for enabled and 0 for
disabled. Do not include spaces around the key or equals sign unless a
particular value explicitly supports them.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Provider selection and transport
.TP
.B provider
Active provider name, commonly openai, gemini, groq, openrouter, mistral,
claude, ollama, or custom.
.TP
.B model
Model identifier sent to the selected provider.
.TP
.B provider_base_url
Base URL for the provider API.
.TP
.B provider_endpoint
API endpoint path or provider-specific endpoint override.
.TP
.B provider_auth_header
Authentication header name used by the configured provider transport.
.TP
.B provider_auth_scheme
Authentication scheme, such as Bearer, where applicable.
.TP
.B provider_query_key
Query parameter name used for providers that authenticate through a query.
.TP
.B provider_api_key_in_query
Set to 1 to send the key as a query parameter when supported; otherwise 0.
.SS Credentials
.TP
.B OPENAI_KEY, GEMINI_KEY, GROQ_KEY, OPENROUTER_KEY, MISTRAL_KEY, CLAUDE_KEY, OLLAMA_KEY, CUSTOM_KEY
Encrypted provider-specific API keys. AITerm uses a master key to decrypt
these values. Keep unused provider keys empty. A legacy api_key entry may be
read for compatibility, but is not written by current versions.
.TP
.B db_pass
Encrypted database password. AITerm also supports AITERM_DB_PASS as a runtime
environment override; treat environment secrets as sensitive.
.SS Database
.TP
.B db_host
MariaDB server host name or address.
.TP
.B db_user
MariaDB account name.
.TP
.B db_name
Database name, normally aiterm_db.
.SS Appearance
.TP
.B color
Enable colorized diagnostic output (1 or 0).
.TP
.B term_transparency
Terminal pane transparency, as a floating-point value.
.TP
.B ai_transparency
AI pane transparency, as a floating-point value.
.TP
.B terminal_font
Font description used by the terminal pane.
.TP
.B ai_font
Font description used by the AI pane.
.SS Runtime toggles
The following values are integer booleans, normally 1 for enabled and 0 for
disabled:
.BR tee_enabled ,
.BR autoreply_enabled ,
.BR auto_execute_enabled ,
.BR ratelimit_enabled ,
.BR smart_cache_enabled ,
.BR noise_filter_enabled ,
.BR debug_mode ,
.BR send_snmp_payload ,
.BR snmp_ticker_enabled ,
.BR xml_tagging ,
.BR ai_retry_enabled ,
.BR load_from_session ,
.BR idle_enabled ,
.BR write_to_global ,
and
.BR read_from_global .
.SS Numeric tuning options
.TP
.B rpm
Requests-per-minute limit for rate limiting.
.TP
.B snmp_poll_interval
SNMP polling interval in seconds.
.TP
.B ai_retry_max_retries
Maximum configured retry count for AI requests.
.TP
.B ai_retry_delay_sec
Delay between AI retry attempts, in seconds.
.TP
.B idle_timeout_minutes
Idle suspension timeout in minutes. The loader accepts values from 0 through
1440; in the current implementation a value of 0 is replaced by the default
of 10 minutes. Idle suspension temporarily disables selected runtime toggles
and restores their prior states when activity resumes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT OVERRIDES
An ordinary configuration key can be overridden by an environment variable
named AITERM_ followed by the uppercase key. For example:
.PP
.nf
AITERM_PROVIDER=gemini
AITERM_IDLE_ENABLED=1
AITERM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=15
AITERM_TERM_TRANSPARENCY=0.85
AITERM_AI_TRANSPARENCY=0.75
.fi
.PP
These values are runtime overrides and are not written to the configuration
file. In the current implementation the override is applied when the matching
configuration entry is read; add the key to the file if it is otherwise
absent. Provider transport variables AITERM_PROVIDER_BASE_URL,
AITERM_PROVIDER_ENDPOINT, AITERM_PROVIDER_AUTH_HEADER,
AITERM_PROVIDER_AUTH_SCHEME, and AITERM_PROVIDER_QUERY_KEY are also supported.
AITERM_CONFIG selects the configuration file, AITERM_MASTER_KEY supplies the
master key, and AITERM_SQL_DIR overrides the SQL initialization directory.
.SH ENCRYPTION
Do not place plaintext API keys or database passwords in the configuration
file. Use the built-in encryption command to generate encrypted values:
.PP
.nf
aiterm --master='your-master-key' --crypt-pw='secret-to-encrypt'
.fi
.PP
The master key is not stored by the application in the configuration file.
If no master key is provided through --master or AITERM_MASTER_KEY, the
application may prompt for it.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
provider=gemini
model=gemini-flash-latest
GEMINI_KEY=<encrypted-value>
db_host=127.0.0.1
db_user=aiterm
db_pass=<encrypted-value>
db_name=aiterm_db
idle_enabled=1
idle_timeout_minutes=10
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I aiterm.conf.example
Example configuration distributed with the source.
.TP
.I /etc/aiterm.conf
System-wide fallback configuration path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aiterm (1),
.BR aiterm-commands (7)
